<mujoco model="embodied-hexapod-spider-18-latched-spring">
  <!-- ADR-202 spider-18: six legs of three STS3215-class position servos each, from the contract hexapod-spec.ts.
       MEDIUM: air (Air (ISA sea level)); the plant takes ONLY gravity from it (ADR-160 D7): no density, no viscosity.
       Body: the two plates as one box of the body mass (0.897 kg), inertia from the layout (six coxa-servo
       lumps at the mounts, the rest a uniform box). Self-collision is OFF (spider geoms collide with the floor only).
       Legs: capsules carrying the mass model's link masses; the tibia thins to a shin over its last 0.03 m so the
       foot sphere is the lowest point of the leg in every pose and a foot contact is a FOOT contact.
       Signs: coxa + = foot forward on every leg (left hinge -z, right +z); femur/tibia + = foot toward body -z.
       Servos: kp = stall / 0.05 rad, damping = stall / no-load speed, armature = the arm's estimate.
       JUMP latched-spring: a double-ended rod on a slide joint along body z (k = 5000 N/m, stroke
       0.038 m, 3.61 J wound) held by the "spring-latch" equality. Wound, the ground-side end sits
       0.01 m below the plate; the plant crouches the legs until that tip rests on the floor, then releases the
       latch and the spring pushes the body up. The winding servo and its cam are not modelled: winding is instantaneous
       on reset (the brief's 2-3 s wind happens between jumps, not during one).
  -->
